  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc / 46.4% F1), which establishes a weak RNA-only baseline. We have no information about whether image features carry discriminative signal for this task. Question being tested: Does the image modality alone provide meaningful classification performance, and how does it compare to the RNA-only baseline? This directly informs the core multimodal hypothesis—without knowing the image-only ceiling, we cannot later attribute any multimodal gain to genuine cross-modal complementarity versus one modality simply being stronger. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the minimal, controlled complement to config_001 (same singleprofile setting, standard resnet50 backbone), giving us both single-modality baselines in just two experiments. This maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (which modality carries signal) before we invest budget in more complex multimodal, multiprofile, or encoder-variant configurations. If image-only is also weak, we know the task is inherently hard and may need better encoders; if it is strong, we know multimodal fusion has a strong partner to complement RNA."
}

